-- title:
--   Characters of the Hecke algebra give mod p cuspidal eigensystems
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $N \ge 1$, a set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, an integer $k$ with $2 \le k$, and a field $F$ of characteristic $p$. Let `heckeAlgebra N k S` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C} S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin k` attached to primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin k` attached to primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, and let $\theta$ be any ring homomorphism from this algebra to $F$. The assertion is that there exist a formal power series $\varphi \in F[\![X]\!]$ and a function $\mathrm{lam} : \mathbb{N} \to F$ such that: $\varphi$ lies in `modPCusp N k F`, the $F$-span of those power series $\operatorname{mk}(n \mapsto (a_n \bmod p))$ arising from a cusp form $f \in S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ and integers $a_n$ with $\mathrm{qCoeff}\, f\, n = a_n$ for all $n$; $\varphi \neq 0$ and, for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, the coefficientwise operator $\mathrm{heckePS}$ sending a series with coefficients $(c_n)$ to the series with $n$-th coefficient $c_{n\ell} + \ell^{k-1} c_{n/\ell}$ (the second term present only when $\ell \mid n$) takes $\varphi$ to $\mathrm{lam}(\ell)\,\varphi$; for all such $\ell$ one has $\mathrm{lam}(\ell) = \theta(T_\ell)$; and for every prime $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ the operator sending a series with coefficients $(c_n)$ to the series with $n$-th coefficient $c_{qn}$ takes $\varphi$ to $\theta(U_q)\,\varphi$.
--
--   This is the reduction half of the Deligne–Serre lifting lemma in characteristic $p$: a character of the anemic Hecke algebra with values in a field of characteristic $p$ is realised by a nonzero mod $p$ cuspidal $q$-expansion whose $T_\ell$- and $U_q$-eigenvalues are the values of the character. It is used in the passage from maximal ideals of the Hecke algebra to mod $p$ eigenforms, by [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_isMaximal_two_ringHom_of_succ_of_map_T_eq_zero_of_five_le_or_exists_prime_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.exists_isMaximal_two_ringHom_of_succ_of_map_T_eq_zero_of_five_le_or_exists_prime_dvd) and by [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.thetaCycle_exists_ringHom_mul_two_apply_eq_of_ringHom_succ_of_eq_three_imp_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.thetaCycle_exists_ringHom_mul_two_apply_eq_of_ringHom_succ_of_eq_three_imp_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
